From: 主理-75 <主理-75@local>
Subject: [PATCH] version.sh: fall back to the packaged version outside a git checkout

tools/version.sh derives the version from `git log --format=format:%D` tag
refs and bails out with `test -d .git || exit` when no git metadata is present.
Both consumers of that script are then handed an empty string:

  * configure.ac: AC_INIT([knxd],m4_esyscmd_s([./tools/version.sh])) -> autoconf
    gets an empty package version (autoreconf/configure cannot name the package);
  * Makefile.am:  version.h -> #define REAL_VERSION "" -> knxd --version prints
    no version at all.

Source tarballs such as the GitHub tag archive carry no .git directory, so print
the packaged version instead of nothing.  Behaviour inside a git checkout is
unchanged, and the Debian-changelog branch above is untouched.

---
 tools/version.sh | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/tools/version.sh
+++ b/tools/version.sh
@@ -7,6 +7,13 @@
     exit
 fi
 
-test -d .git || exit
+if ! test -d .git ; then
+	# Not a git checkout (source/tarball build): the packaged version is the
+	# only truth available here.  Both consumers of this script --
+	# configure.ac AC_INIT(m4_esyscmd_s) and Makefile.am version.h -- would
+	# otherwise receive an empty string and produce a version-less knxd.
+	echo 0.14.73
+	exit
+fi
 # git describe --tags
 git log --format=format:%D | perl -ne 'next unless s#.*tag: ##; s#,.*##; next if m#/#; print; exit;'
